From a6df20cbc4ab56aa2932215fc9ce1d925de5bbe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sivan <zifanuu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 12:41:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(mcp): attempt streamable-http OAuth silently by
 default
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Requiring an explicit auth declaration stranded every suite whose
author never added one — a freshly installed Figma MCP had no path to
the browser flow and no user-facing way to know an override existed.
The provider now attaches by default: it only activates on the server's
401 challenge, so servers without auth are untouched, and a static
Authorization header (a token flow) or auth.enabled: false opts out.
Schema default flipped to enabled; READMEs, gate tests, and the agent
note record the semantics.
